A simple memory trick

Think of the names:

Lower Bound → the lowest (leftmost) place where x could go without violating sorted order. That means the first element ≥ x.
Upper Bound → the first position after all occurrences of x, i.e., the first element > x.

Find the first position where this number can be inserted without breaking the sorted order.: lower bound